# TypeScript source, JavaScript clients

The library is written in TypeScript and must run from plain JavaScript.

- Implement library code in TypeScript under `src/`.
- Export functions and plain data as named exports from `src/index.ts`.
- Callers must be able to build arguments with objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, and functions.
- Use string unions. Do not add `enum` or `namespace`.
- A JavaScript caller must not need a class instance or a TypeScript-only wrapper to use the API.
- Build ESM (`dist/index.js`) and CommonJS (`dist/index.cjs`), and ship declaration files.
- Keep the `package.json` `exports` map pointed at those build artifacts.
- When the public API changes, update the JavaScript examples under `examples/`.

```javascript
import { ok, map } from "tirjs";

const result = map(ok(2), (n) => n + 1);
```

```javascript
const { ok, map } = require("tirjs");
```
